       hand-authored: the whole string must parse; nothing is dumped on a bad one.

== paste (6 cases) ==
  PASS merges corresponding lines of each file, TAB by default -- The default output ... shall be the concatenation of the corresponding lines ... separated by a <tab>.
  PASS a shorter file contributes an empty field, not a shorter row -- When the end of one file is reached before the end of the other(s), for each subsequent line, ... a null string shall be used in place of the missing input.
  PASS -d changes the delimiter (single character) -- -d list -- Use one or more of the characters in ... list, instead of the default <tab>.
  PASS -s serializes each file's own lines into one row -- -s -- Concatenate all of the lines from each input file into one line of output per file.
  PASS at least one file operand is required -- SYNOPSIS -- paste [-s] [-d list] file...
       hand-authored: paste.s's own :usageerr2 path -- exit 2 is this tree's uniform usage-error convention. This host's own paste with no operand also refuses, exit 1 -- a different but also nonzero exit, not host-oracled because of that mismatch.
  PASS '-' as an operand means standard input -- A <hyphen-minus> ... shall be used to instruct paste to read from standard input in that position in the list of file operands.

== patch (12 cases) ==
  PASS a unified diff is detected and applied -- The patch utility shall read a source (patch) file containing any of the three forms of difference (diff) listing produced by the diff utility... and apply those differences
       hand-authored: stdout is not the assertion here -- see this module's own docstring: patch(1) reports itself on stdout in words BSD and GNU spell differently, maux reports on fd 2 instead, and the specified behaviour is the CONTENT of the files, which results= compares. The expected contents below were produced by running this host's own /usr/bin/patch over the same fixture and argv, not captured from maux.
  PASS a context diff is detected and applied -- ...any of the three forms of difference (diff) listing produced by the diff utility
